Id: time004w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_timesync
Fix: Keep one daemon; turn the others off (systemctl disable --now on Linux, _enable="NO" in rc.conf on FreeBSD).
References: chronyd(8); systemd-timesyncd(8); rc.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

More than one time synchronisation daemon is running. Each corrects
the clock towards its own servers, so they fight, and the clock can
jump back and forth. It usually happens when chrony or ntpd was
installed on a system where another daemon was already on
(systemd-timesyncd on Linux, timed on macOS).

To fix it, keep one and turn the others off: 'systemctl disable --now
systemd-timesyncd' when chrony is the one to keep on Linux,
_enable="NO" in rc.conf on FreeBSD, and on macOS stop what should not
run beside timed.
